    14	## Attack 1: CARLA-clean is a rendering-pipeline confound, not demonstrated "distribution shift," and the parity argument does not cover it
    15	
    16	- CLASS: uncontrolled confound (the central one).
    17	- TARGET (draft location): Abstract, "Running the verified model on CARLA-rendered clean
    18	  roads, we find that it fails silently"; Section 1, "On CARLA-rendered clean roads, 8 of 10
    19	  of the model's output heads collapse"; Section 4 Method, "The out-of-distribution data are
    20	  CARLA-rendered clean-road frames from the openpilot v0.9.7 simulation pipeline." The entire
    21	  load-bearing phenomenon (E1, E2, E3) rests on this single OOD source.
    22	- THE ATTACK: The paper's whole negative finding is "a production model fails silently under
    23	  visual OOD," but the only OOD axis that induces the collapse is CARLA-clean frames. The
    24	  paper never rules out the mundane explanation: CARLA renders with different camera
    25	  intrinsics, different field-of-view, different tone-mapping/gamma, no lens distortion, no
    26	  rolling-shutter, no sensor noise, and a synthetic color/texture distribution. A frozen
    27	  network fed input from a pipeline whose geometry and photometry it never saw at train time
    28	  will of course produce garbage. That is not "the model fails to perceive a valid driving
    29	  scene"; it is "the input was fed through the wrong camera model." The parity argument
    30	  (Section 4) proves only that the harness reproduces comma's output on REAL frames; it says
    31	  nothing about whether the CARLA frames were geometrically and photometrically conditioned
    32	  the way comma's own simulation pipeline conditions them. E7 makes this worse, not better:
    33	  Section 5.7 shows that NO photometric or blur corruption of real frames reproduces the
    34	  collapse ("0 of 75 cells"), which means the trigger is something specific to the full-sim
    35	  rendering pipeline, exactly the camera-model/geometry confound, and not a general property
    36	  of "out-of-distribution input." The reviewer's one-line kill: "You have shown the model
    37	  breaks on one renderer's output. You have not shown it breaks on out-of-distribution
    38	  driving scenes."
    39	- EVIDENCE: The contract itself concedes the scope: "one extreme OOD axis (CARLA) plus one
    40	  bounding axis (ImageNet-C)" and parks "a second, real adverse-weather OOD axis ... that
    41	  actually induces a non-CARLA output collapse" as "the most reviewer-resistant follow-up"
    42	  (contribution_contract.md, out-of-scope). The Limitations section concedes "no non-CARLA
    43	  output collapse was ever induced." The draft asserts the collapse is "downstream of the
    44	  vision encoder" (E5), which is the only structural fact that pushes back on the
    45	  camera-intrinsics story, BUT the draft never measures the obvious confound directly: it
    46	  never reports whether the CARLA frames were passed through comma's documented sim camera
