   256	- THE ATTACK: A reviewer who recomputes ANY number and finds it off will distrust EVERY
   257	  number. Two are flagged in the stats audit. (a) The draft's frame count is internally
   258	  inconsistent: it says 0 of 219 in the Abstract but the Method section's "320 minus 100"
   259	  arithmetic implies 220, and the npz actually stores 319 (post-warmup 219). (b) The "AUROC
   260	  crosses 0.5 at the same alpha=0.550" claim is simply false: the stats audit recomputed AUROC
   261	  = 0.400 at alpha=0.425 and 0.540 at alpha=0.450, so AUROC crosses 0.5 near alpha=0.45, about
   262	  0.10 alpha-units BEFORE the fire-fraction crossing at 0.550. The draft overstates the
   263	  coherence of the two metrics to make the early-warning story look tighter than it is.
   264	- EVIDENCE: Stats audit c11 / IC-1 (FLAGGED): "The draft's '0 of 220' should read '0 of 219'
   265	  ... the actual npz gives 219." Stats audit c31 / IC-6 (FLAGGED, FAIL): "the 'same alpha'
   266	  claim is incorrect by approximately 0.10 alpha units ... AUROC actually crosses 0.5 ~0.10
   267	  alpha units earlier than the fire-fraction." Both are confirmed by recomputation, not
